      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kiryat_Bialik"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Kiryat Bialik takes its name from the celebrated poet Hayim Nahman Bialik, honoring his literary legacy.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2,
        8
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia",
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kiryat_Bialik"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "After becoming a local council in 1950, Kiryat Bialik achieved city status in 1976, marking its growth.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        22
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kiryat_Bialik"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Every May, the city hosts the Bialik Festival for Literature and Poetry, drawing authors, concerts, and children’s plays.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        13
